/openwizdev/OpenWiz/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/deployments","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:55:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T11:09:07Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-24T14:31:38Z","git_url":"git://github.com/openwizdev/OpenWiz.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:openwizdev/OpenWiz.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/OpenWiz.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/OpenWiz","homepage":"https://openwiz.dev","size":37849,"stargazers_count":8,"watchers_count":8,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":586,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-factory","agent-orchestration","ai","ai-agents","automation","claude-code","cli","cloudroom","code-review","codex","coding-agents","developer-tools","github","kernel","llm","multi-agent","open-source","openclaw","rust","software-factory"],"visibility":"public","forks":1,"open_issues":586,"watchers":8,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"body":"## Parent\n\nTicket BK2 of spec #2963: the booking API on Cloudflare Pages Functions. Size: L.\n\n**Base branch:** `book` in `openwizdev/WizSite` (the integration branch for spec #2963). Open the pull request against `book`, never `main`: a merge to `main` deploys the site, and that waits for the maintainer.\n\n**Rules:** no new npm dependency; Node.js 24 standard library and the Workers runtime only (`fetch`, `crypto.subtle`, `Intl`); follow `contracts/comments.v1.md`; no secret, real email address or real calendar data in code, tests, fixtures or logs.\n\n## What to build\n\nThe four routes of the spec's contract (`openwiz.book.v1`), exactly as the spec states them, on top of BK1's `lib/book/ical.js`, `slots.js`, `fake.js` and BK3's `lib/book/mail.js`, `google.js` (already on `book`; read them, do not change them):\n\n- `functions/api/book/slots.js` (`GET`), `functions/api/book/index.js` (`POST /api/book`), `functions/api/book/cancel.js` (`POST`), `functions/api/book/feed.js` (`GET`). Each exports `onRequest` and a testable `handle(request, env, {fetch, now})`. Other methods get `405`.\n- **Busy time:** mode `fake` uses `fakeBusy`; mode `live` uses `googleBusy` when `googleReady(env)`, else fetches `BOOK_ICAL_URL` (https only, 10 s timeout, at most 2 MB, no redirects off https) through `busyFromIcal`. Mode `off`, missing settings, a missing database or any read failure answers `503 unavailable`. The iCal address is a secret: never in a response, error or log.\n- **Storage** (`lib/book/store.js`): D1 at `env.BOOK_DB ?? env.ASK_A_WIZ_COUNTERS`. Tables created on first use: `book_bookings (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, start INTEGER, end INTEGER, name, email, team, tz, status, cancel_hash, google_event, created INTEGER)` with a unique index on `start` where `status = 'booked'`, and `book_limits (day TEXT, key TEXT, count INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY (day, key))`. Every store call has a 5 s timeout.\n- **Booking:** same-origin `Origin`, `Content-Type: application/json`, body at most 4 KB, exactly the contract's keys, the field limits of the spec, a plausible single email address. A filled `website` honeypot answers the normal `200` shape with a made-up id and stores and sends nothing. Then: rate limits, then re-read busy time and bookings and accept `start` only if `openSlots` offers it now (else `409 slot_taken`), then insert (a unique-index conflict is `409 slot_taken`), then `googleInsert` when ready (best effort; keep the event id), then `sendBookingMail` (its result is the answer's `email`). The id is 16 random bytes, base64url; the cancel token is 32 random bytes, stored only as its SHA-256; the cancel link is `https://<this origin>/book/?cancel=<id>.<token>`.\n- **Rate limits** (D1 counters keyed by a daily-salted hash of `CF-Connecting-IP`, as `functions/api/ask.js` does; never the raw address): slots 120 an hour per visitor; booking attempts 10 an hour per visitor; bookings 3 a day per visitor, 2 upcoming per email address, 20 a day overall. Over a limit: `429 rate_limited` with `Retry-After`.\n- **Cancel:** constant-time token check; marks the row `cancelled` (the slot opens again), `googleDelete` when there is an event, `sendCancelMail`. Unknown id, wrong token or a past booking: `404 not_found`. A second cancel: `200`.\n- **Feed:** as the contract says; constant-time compare; never cached.\n- `scripts/book-dev.mjs`: a local preview server with no dependency: serves `dist/` and routes `/api/book/*` to the handlers with an in-memory `node:sqlite` database behind a D1-shaped wrapper, `BOOK_MODE=fake` by default, `--port` (default 8801), bound to 127.0.0.1. It sends no email and calls no outside service unless the matching environment variables are set.\n- `package.json`: add `tests/book-*.test.mjs` to `test:functions`.\n- `docs/maintaining.md`: one short section, *Booking*: the routes, every setting and secret by name with its default, and the switch.\n\n## Owned paths\n\n- `functions/api/book/`, `lib/book/store.js`, `scripts/book-dev.mjs` in `openwizdev/WizSite`\n- `tests/book-api.test.mjs` in `openwizdev/WizSite`\n- `package.json` (shared: the `test:functions` line only), `docs/maintaining.md` (shared: the Booking section only)\n\n**Relies on:** BK1, BK3 (merged to `book`)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Red first, then green: `npm run test:functions`, with a `node:sqlite` fake D1 as `tests/ask.test.mjs` does: every status in the contract, each rate limit, the honeypot, a double booking of one slot (two requests, one `409`), a slot outside hours or inside a buffer refused, cancel then rebook, the feed's three answers, a calendar read failure (`503`, nothing leaked), a D1 failure and timeout\n- [ ] No response, error or log line carries the iCal address, a token or a raw IP address (asserted in tests)\n- [ ] `npm run build && npm run check && npm test` still pass; `node scripts/book-dev.mjs` serves slots and takes a booking in fake mode\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/issues/2966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/OpenWiz/issues/2966/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"jparker2006","id":85816763,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODE2NzYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserco